ased to exist after it was defeated and surrendered to the British Empire at the end of the Second Boer War in 1902. It is one of the three historical precursors to the present-day Free State province.\nExtending between the Orange and Vaal rivers, its borders were determined by the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland in 1848 when the region was proclaimed as the Orange River Sovereignty, with a British Resident based in Bloemfontein. Bloemfontein and the southern parts of the Sovereignty had previously been settled by Griqua and by Trekboere from the Cape Colony."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q218023","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q37701","value_label":"Bloemfontein","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Bloemfontein"},{"qid":"Q218023","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q7411","value_label":"Dutch","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Dutch"},{"qid":"Q218023","kind":"religion","value_qid":"Q2075119","value_label":"Nederduitse Gereformeerde Kerk","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P140","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Nederduitse Gereformeerde Kerk"},{"qid":"Q218023","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q7270","value_label":"republic","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"republic"},{"qid":"Q218023","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q3048062","value_label":"Orange River Sovereignty","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1365","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Orange River Sovereignty"},{"qid":"Q218023","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q1142179","value_label":"Orange River Colony","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1366","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Orange River Colony"},{"qid":"Q218023","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flag of the Orange Free State.svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q218023","kin